{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He found him in a desert land.</b> Like יַמְצִיאֶהוּ — that He provided for them all their needs, such as the well and the manna with which their clothes did not wear out and their feet did not swell." "<b>And in the howling waste of a wilderness.</b> In that desolation of the wilderness, which is a place of barrenness and howling — for there is nothing there except jackals and ostriches that mourn and howl, as it is said: ״אעשה מספד כתנים״ etc. — there He provided all their needs, and so Onkelos translates. Another explanation: ימצאהו בארץ מדבר — a great find did Israel find in the wilderness: the Torah, which was given to them there." "<b>And in the howling waste of a wilderness.</b> For before the Torah was given, the world was dark and desolate like the night, and when it was given it was light, as it is said: ״כי נר מצוה ותורה אור״." "<b>He encompassed him.</b> With a shelter of clouds. Another explanation: at Mount Sinai, when He suspended the mountain over them like a tub." "<b>He instructed him.</b> That He gave them understanding in the Torah. Another explanation: the language of building — the Tabernacle." "<b>He encompassed him as the apple of His eye.</b> That He protected them from the nations and from Amalek."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:47.996553539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}